<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime exception for the cc_server executable (Dart AOT, built by
  `dart build cli`).

  NB: no double hyphen may appear anywhere in this comment. XML forbids the
  sequence inside comments and while plutil tolerates it, the AMFI parser
  inside codesign does not: "Failed to parse entitlements: AMFIUnserializeXML:
  syntax error". So codesign flags are written here with a single dash.

  The standalone Dart runtime maps the AOT snapshot embedded in its own binary
  as executable memory at startup. The hardened runtime forbids that mapping
  without this exception and the kernel kills the process on its first
  snapshot instruction:

    Termination Reason: CODESIGNING 2 Invalid Page
    signal: SIGKILL (Code Signature Invalid)

  The cruel part: such a binary passes codesign's strict verification
  (-verify -strict), sails through notarization and then dies instantly on
  every launch. v0.0.1 shipped exactly that; the desktop sat in the Dock with
  no window, waiting forever on a server that was SIGKILLed at spawn. Verified
  A/B on the shipped binary: hardened + bare = SIGKILL, hardened + this
  entitlement = runs. This is the documented signing requirement for
  standalone Dart AOT executables, not a bypass.

  Applied to the cc_server executable only. Entitlements are read from a
  process's main executable, so the dylibs beside it take none. The JIT and
  library-validation exceptions node needs (code_server.entitlements) are NOT
  needed here: Dart AOT never JITs and cc_server only loads dylibs signed
  with the same Developer ID.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
